    "cleo_faq_page_eNRzkb": {
      "type": "cleo-faq-page",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_h4Gahq": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I tell my Neera is real copper?",
            "answer": "<p>Every Neera is solid copper with no plating, lining or coating, and an independent SGS lab test measured over 99.9% copper. Two quick checks at home: a magnet will not stick to it, as it would to plated steel, and the inside darkens within a week or two of daily use, which a lacquered or lined bottle never does. Each piece is shaped and hammered by hand, so small variations in shape and surface are part of its character. If anything on your Neera looks wrong, send us a photo and we will help.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_kcfV76": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is my copper bottle changing color, or turning green?",
            "answer": "<p>Darkening and green spots are both natural: real copper reacting with water, moisture and air. Green is copper oxidation, not mold, and it is a sign of genuine, bare copper. To bring back the shine, swirl a tablespoon of lemon juice or tamarind with a teaspoon of salt inside for two minutes, rinse until the water runs clear and dry it with a soft cloth. Clean any green away before the next fill, and never drink water with a blue tint.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_BetJec": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The cap's O-ring or threading doesn't seem to align perfectly. How can I fix this?",
            "answer": "<p>Because every bottle is handcrafted, the threads and the silicone O-ring can need a short break-in period. Press down evenly on the cap and twist it slowly so the threads find their path, and make sure the O-ring sits completely flat inside the cap. Closed snugly, the cap is leak-resistant.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_AMh8Rh": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I keep my Neera in the refrigerator?",
            "answer": "<p>We recommend room-temperature or cool water and no fridge or freezer. For a chilled drink, fill it with cool water right before you head out. Never freeze it: water expands as it freezes and can deform the handcrafted copper.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_tzNaRp": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where is Neera based, and where do you ship from?",
            "answer": "<p>Neera is a US brand. Every bottle is handcrafted in India and ships from our warehouse in the United States, with free shipping on every US order.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_FXPJkf": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I track my order?",
            "answer": "<p>As soon as your order ships, you receive an email with your tracking number and a direct link to follow it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_p7L7JA": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I change my shipping address after placing an order?",
            "answer": "<p>We process and dispatch orders promptly. If you need to update your address, contact our support team right away. We can change it as long as the package has not left our warehouse; once it is with the courier, we can no longer reroute it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_QVaiHa": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I received an incomplete order. How will this be resolved?",
            "answer": "<p>We are sorry for the mix-up. Contact our support team with your order number and we will ship the missing items as quickly as possible. You will receive a new tracking number by email as soon as they leave our warehouse.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_chNDET": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I received the wrong order. What are the next steps?",
            "answer": "<p>We are sorry for the mix-up. Send our support team a clear photo of the items you received, and we will send your correct order and arrange the return of the wrong items at no cost to you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_gfCCDA": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My tracking status hasn't updated in a few days. Should I be concerned?",
            "answer": "<p>Usually not. Tracking can pause while a package moves between sorting hubs. If your status has not changed for more than five business days, contact our support team and we will look into it with the carrier.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_bmfDPU": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What inspires Neera?",
            "answer": "<p>Neera began with a simple belief: everyday drinkware can carry a tradition. In Ayurveda, water that rests overnight in copper is called tamra jal, and families across India have kept their drinking water in copper for centuries. Neera brings that ritual into modern homes, made the honest way: solid copper, shaped and hammered by hand in India, and tested by an independent lab.</p>"
          }
        }
